  "configuration_id": "config_027",
  "reason": "Evidence: The current best is config_039 (scvi_n200 + imagenet_vit_l + transformer + weighted, 0.725 acc). In RNA-only settings, scvi_n200 substantially outperforms pca_n2000 (0.653 vs 0.591, ~6 pts), but we have no data on whether this RNA-encoder gap persists when a strong image encoder is present. Question tested: Does the RNA encoder choice (scvi_n200 vs pca_n2000) still materially affect multimodal performance, or does the ViT-L image encoder dominate the signal? Why this is the best next experiment: config_027 changes exactly one variable (RNA encoder) from the current best (config_039), giving a clean ablation. If performance is close to 0.725, it reveals the image carries most of the predictive signal and the RNA pipeline can be simplified, freeing budget for other design choices. If it drops substantially, it confirms scvi_n200 is essential and we should focus remaining budget on optimizing around that encoder. This high-information experiment is more valuable than testing minor variations (e.g., avgpool vs transformer, which showed negligible difference in RNA-only) under the limited budget."
}

